    "narrative": "Our lineup optimization for June 2nd centers on **Jackson Merrill** (62.21) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.57) as our primary anchors. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Aaron Nola, where his favorable platoon split and projected order placement elevate his efficiency despite Nola\u2019s pedigree. **Kyle Tucker** (61.21) also remains a cornerstone play against Soroka; while his raw projections are slightly tempered by SP skill, his elite batted-ball profile and position in the heart of the order keep him well within the \"Strong\" start tier. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (60.31) provides the highest volatility-to-upside ratio today, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Bachar allows him to transcend his base projection and serve as a crucial engine for our stolen base and batting average needs.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Coby Mayo** (47.33) in favor of the existing UTIL configuration. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from a strong park factor against Early, his efficiency is capped by the SP\u2019s strikeout capability, ultimately leaving him just shy of the threshold set by **Miguel Vargas** (56.18), who carries a more favorable plate appearance projection due to his high-leverage spot in the order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gunnar Henderson** (50.05); while he is a must-start talent, today\u2019s matchup against Early represents a significant efficiency tax, and his performance will be the primary barometer for whether we maintain our scoring pace against left-handed starters. As a final note, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined, ensuring that our depth\u2014though tested\u2014stays focused on maximizing every game cap for the categories of HR and SB.",
